    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d957">

                <pb facs="1104" n="1008" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1008"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Mr. Woodford.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-02-09"><hi rendition="#italic">February 9,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>There has appeared in the public prints a letter, addressed early in December
                    last by the Spanish minister to Mr. Canalejas, and which the minister admits was
                    written by him. It contains expressions concerning the President of the United
                    States of such character as to end the minister’s utility as a medium for frank
                    and sincere intercourse between this country and Spain. You are, therefore,
                    instructed to at once say to the minister of state that the immediate recall of
                    the minister is expected by the President.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Day</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acting.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
